! Nearest-neighbour fragment construction for quartz at level 1.
!
! The assertion is partly in the file NAMES: put_atom_group_mols names each
! fragment "group-<n>-<chemical formula>", so if the fragmentation is wrong
! the declared output simply does not exist and the test fails, rather than
! comparing wrong numbers against a reference.
!
! group-1-H4O4Si is orthosilicic acid and group-2-H6OSi2 is silyloxysilane,
! which is what Davidson (2023) Fig. 5.2 says the level 1 fragments are.
!
! Only the .xyz files are compared. The un-suffixed group-* files are the
! full molecule dumps, which carry basis set detail irrelevant to fragment
! geometry.
!
! quartz_init.cif is the structure from Quartz1_CD.cif (Olex2/SHELXL,
! 16 Jan 2024, Ag Ka, 100 K -- Bern, Balmohammadi, via Grabowsky) with the
! 162822 embedded reflections stripped. NOTE it is NOT the reduction used
! in the thesis, which merged to 1134 unique reflections against this one's
! 1748, so absolute R factors from this structure will not reproduce the
! thesis tables. Fragment geometry does not depend on the reduction.

   input:   quartz_init.cif

   output:  group-1-H4O4Si.xyz
   output:  group-2-H6OSi2.xyz

   delete:  group-1-H4O4Si
   delete:  group-2-H6OSi2
